ion":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds is having an MRI on his injured knee, and backup Christopher Vizzina was sent to the hospital to evaluate his ankle.","published":"2026-11-14T23:52:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T22:28:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State WR Smith sets Big Ten record, states Heisman case","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards while also making his Heisman Trophy case in Saturday's win over Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T23:15:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870874/lawson-luckie","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawson_Luckie"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Lawson Luckie","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawson_Luckie","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:23Z","intro":"Lawson Luckie (born October 21, 2004) is an American college football tight end for the Georgia Bulldogs of the Southeastern Conference (SEC).","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Luckie grew up in Norcross, Georgia, and attended Norcross High School. He accumulated 728 all-purpose yards as a senior. Luckie was rated a four-star recruit and committed to play college football at Georgia over offers from Alabama, Auburn, Florida State, LSU, Ole Miss, and Texas A&M."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Luckie joined the Georgia Bulldogs as an early enrollee in December 2022 and took part in the team's practices leading up to the 2022 Peach Bowl. He played in seven games as a true freshman and caught two passes for nine yards and one touchdown."}]}}